# Ship-gate workflow

Start and finish product work from a Cursor agent request. Do not auto-merge, auto-deploy, create a GitHub Release, or edit sibling website changelogs without an explicit user choice at each gate.

## Gates

At each gate, end the turn with a numbered list of next best actions and **one recommended reply**. Wait for the user before continuing.

### After PR CI is green

Recommended usually: merge when release metadata and checks are OK.

1. Merge the PR
2. Fix remaining review / CI issues
3. Leave PR open / stop

Never merge unless the user already ordered merge or picks option 1.

### After merge is verified on `main`

Recommended: deploy when main tests are green.

1. Deploy to Cloudron now
2. Skip deploy

Never assume Cloudron already updated. Deploy only via `workflow_dispatch` (see `.cursor/skills/ship-gate/SKILL.md`).

### After Cloudron deploy succeeds — changelog hubs

App Change Log Hub (`/change-log`) is fed by `resources/data/releases.json` in **this** repo. A successful Cloudron deploy publishes that record; do not open a separate metadata PR for the hub.

Recommended: verify the live app hub, then ask about sibling websites only if the user wants them updated.

1. Verify app Change Log Hub on live, then continue to GitHub Release gate
2. Also update sibling website changelogs / hubs (name which sites after the user confirms)
3. Skip hub checks

Never edit `APESCIC/*` website repos or create issues there unless the user explicitly asks in this session.

### After changelog gate — GitHub Release

Recommended: create a GitHub Release for the new `VERSION`.

1. Create GitHub Release
2. Skip release

Never create the release silently.

## Unchanged

Release **metadata** (`VERSION`, `releases.json`, contract) still ships in the **same PR** before merge (see release-metadata rule). That metadata is the source of truth for the MyAPES Core Change Log Hub after deploy.
